1
00:03:55,199 --> 00:04:01,199
More minions. More despicable.

2
00:07:50,399 --> 00:07:56,399
Despicable Me 2 is a animation, comedy, family film directed by Chris Renaud.

3
00:11:45,599 --> 00:11:51,599
Gru is recruited by the Anti-Villain League to help
deal with a powerful new super criminal.

4
00:15:40,799 --> 00:15:46,799
Gru (voice), played by Steve Carell.

5
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:42,000
Lucy (voice), played by Kristen Wiig.

6
00:23:31,199 --> 00:23:37,199
Eduardo/El Macho (voice), played by Benjamin Bratt.

7
00:27:26,399 --> 00:27:32,399
Margo (voice), played by Miranda Cosgrove.

8
00:31:21,599 --> 00:31:27,599
Edith (voice), played by Dana Gaier.

9
00:35:16,799 --> 00:35:22,799
Agnes (voice), played by Elsie Fisher.

10
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:18,000
Despicable Me 2 is a 2013 American animated comedy film directed by Chris
Renaud and Pierre Coffin and written by Cinco Paul and Ken Daurio.

11
00:43:07,199 --> 00:43:13,199
Produced by Illumination Entertainment and distributed by Universal Pictures, it is the
second installment in the Despicable Me franchise, following the 2010 film.

12
00:47:02,399 --> 00:47:08,399
The film stars the voices of Steve Carell, Kristen Wiig, Benjamin Bratt,
Miranda Cosgrove, Russell Brand, Steve Coogan, and Ken Jeong.

13
00:50:57,599 --> 00:51:03,599
In the film, secret agent Lucy Wilde recruits retired supervillain Gru to investigate the theft
of a powerful mutagen by El Macho, a supervillain who pursues world domination.

14
00:54:52,799 --> 00:54:58,799
Development of Despicable Me 2 began in 2010 following the success of the
original film, with the directors, producers, and writers returning.

15
00:58:48,000 --> 00:58:54,000
Production was underway by February 2012, with the majority of the cast returning to voice the characters, along
with new cast members, while animation services were provided by Illumination Mac Guff in France.

16
01:02:43,199 --> 01:02:49,199
Al Pacino was cast as the voice of El Macho, recording all of his dialogue, but left in May 2013 over creative differences; Bratt
was brought in to replace Pacino, and used him as an inspiration after finding imitating his voice impossible.

17
01:06:38,399 --> 01:06:44,399
Heitor Pereira and Pharrell Williams returned for the sequel's music.

18
01:10:33,599 --> 01:10:39,599
Despicable Me 2 premiered in Australia on June 5, 2013, and was
theatrically released in the United States on July 3.

19
01:14:28,800 --> 01:14:34,800
It received generally positive reviews from critics,
who praised its humor and animation.

20
01:18:24,000 --> 01:18:30,000
It earned $971 million worldwide, becoming the third-highest-grossing film of 2013
and the most profitable film for Universal Pictures at the time.

21
01:22:19,199 --> 01:22:25,199
It was nominated for two awards at the 86th Academy
Awards, and received numerous other accolades.

22
01:26:14,399 --> 01:26:20,399
A sequel, Despicable Me 3, was released in 2017.

23
01:30:09,599 --> 01:30:15,599
The film explores themes of parent child relationship,
villain, adoptive father, secret agent, bakery.

24
01:34:04,799 --> 01:34:10,799
The tone is lighthearted.
